@page
@model RROMS.Web.Pages.Dev.StyleGuideModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Design system";
}

<header class="rr-page-header">
    <div>
        <span class="rr-label">Development only</span>
        <h1>RROMS design system</h1>
        <p class="rr-lede">
            The look of a kopitiam: the painted signboard over the door, mint wall tiles, marble tabletops, white
            enamel, and the docket that goes to the kitchen. Build every page from these pieces. DESIGN.md in the
            repo has the rules and the markup.
        </p>
    </div>
</header>

<nav class="nav nav-pills mb-5" aria-label="On this page">
    <a class="nav-link" href="#principles">Principles</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#signboard">Signboard</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#colour">Colour</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#type">Type</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#words">Words</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#buttons">Buttons</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#status">Status</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#forms">Forms</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#dockets">Dockets</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#board">Order rail</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#lists">Lists</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#dashboards">Dashboards</a>
    <a class="nav-link" href="#pieces">Page pieces</a>
</nav>

<section class="sg-section" id="principles">
    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <ul class="sg-principles">
        <li><strong>One action colour.</strong> Pandan green is for things people can do: buttons, links, the option they chose. Status colours describe a state and are never pressed.</li>
        <li><strong>Records are dockets.</strong> Anything that changes hands (a booking, an order, a receipt) is shown as a paper docket with its reference number in monospace.</li>
        <li><strong>Two densities.</strong> Customers get one comfortable column and big tap targets, with the main action at the bottom on a phone. Staff get the full width and an action beside each row.</li>
        <li><strong>Summary before detail.</strong> Lead with what needs attention (what's pending, what's ready), then the rest.</li>
        <li><strong>Real content only.</strong> Real dishes, prices in RM, and real statuses. No placeholder text, no invented figures.</li>
        <li><strong>One bold thing.</strong> The signboard header is the one decoration, on every page. Below it the docket is the only paper; everything else stays plain: no gradients, no extra shadows.</li>
        <li><strong>Say it in words.</strong> "Table 3 for 2 people", "2 bookings for 8 people, 1 to confirm". No dot-separated strings, and labels in sentence case, never capitals.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="signboard">
    <h2>Signboard</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
        The header at the top of this page: deep signboard green, the name in gilt Zilla Slab, and a row of mint wall
        tiles under it. The current page gets a gilt bar under its link (beside it in the phone menu), and keyboard
        focus on the sign shows in gilt. It comes from <code>_Layout.cshtml</code>; pages never add their own. Gilt is
        only for lettering on the sign, never on white.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="colour">
    <h2>Colour</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">Use the tokens (<code>var(--rr-pandan)</code>) or the Bootstrap classes, which already use them (<code>btn-primary</code>, <code>text-bg-warning</code>, <code>alert-danger</code>).</p>
    <div class="sg-swatches">
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#eef1ee"></span><strong>Marble</strong><code>--rr-marble</code><span class="rr-ref">#EEF1EE</span><span>Page background, the tabletop.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#ffffff"></span><strong>Enamel</strong><code>--rr-enamel</code><span class="rr-ref">#FFFFFF</span><span>Cards, dockets, forms.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#1d1a17"></span><strong>Kopi-O</strong><code>--rr-kopi</code><span class="rr-ref">#1D1A17</span><span>Text and headings.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#0b6b4f"></span><strong>Pandan</strong><code>--rr-pandan</code><span class="rr-ref">#0B6B4F</span><span>Actions, links, chosen options, focus, confirmed and ready.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#143b2f"></span><strong>Signboard</strong><code>--rr-signboard</code><span class="rr-ref">#143B2F</span><span>The header, and the top of a date block.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#d4a72c"></span><strong>Gilt</strong><code>--rr-gilt</code><span class="rr-ref">#D4A72C</span><span>Lettering on the signboard only.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#b9dccd"></span><strong>Tile</strong><code>--rr-tile</code><span class="rr-ref">#B9DCCD</span><span>The wall tiles under the sign.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#e9b23c"></span><strong>Kaya</strong><code>--rr-kaya</code><span class="rr-ref">#E9B23C</span><span>Needs attention: pending, new. A fill or an edge, never text on white.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#a86b3c"></span><strong>Teh</strong><code>--rr-teh</code><span class="rr-ref">#A86B3C</span><span>Being worked on: preparing.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#c2381c"></span><strong>Sambal</strong><code>--rr-sambal</code><span class="rr-ref">#C2381C</span><span>Cancel, errors, refusals.</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><span class="sg-chip" style="background:#d8dcd7"></span><strong>Line</strong><code>--rr-line</code><span class="rr-ref">#D8DCD7</span><span>Borders and rules. Secondary text is <span class="rr-ref">#5D625C</span>.</span></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="type">
    <h2>Type</h2>
    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-lg-7">
            <div class="sg-demo">
                <span class="rr-label">Display: Zilla Slab, for headings, times, table numbers and the wordmark</span>
                <p class="h1 mt-2">Book a table, then order from it.</p>
                <p class="h2">Manage reservations</p>
                <p class="h3 mb-0">Table 6</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-5">
            <div class="sg-demo h-100">
                <span class="rr-label">Body: Plus Jakarta Sans, for everything else</span>
                <p class="mt-2">Reserve a lunch or dinner seating ahead. Once you're sitting down, order from your phone.</p>
                <span class="rr-label">References and money</span>
                <p class="mt-2 mb-0"><span class="rr-ref">ORD-001257</span> and <span class="rr-money">RM 26.90</span> on a page; on a docket the reference prints in monospace.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3 mb-0">Sizes step by 1.25: 13, 14, 16, 20, 25, 31 and 39px, and 61px for the front page's headline. Headings use <code>h1</code>–<code>h3</code> (slab). Small labels use <code>rr-label</code>: bold, sentence case, only for real labels such as "Special request" or "Lunch". References use <code>rr-ref</code>; money uses <code>rr-money</code> so the digits line up.</p>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="words">
    <h2>Words</h2>
    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <ul class="sg-rules">
                <li>Buttons say what happens: <strong>Book table</strong>, <strong>Start preparing</strong>, <strong>Cancel booking</strong>. Never "Submit" or "OK".</li>
                <li>Sentence case everywhere: "Manage reservations", not "Manage Reservations".</li>
                <li>After an action, say what happened: "RES-001840 is now confirmed."</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <ul class="sg-rules">
                <li>Errors say what went wrong and what to do next: "That table is already booked for this seating. Choose another time or table."</li>
                <li>Formats: <span class="rr-money">RM 85.50</span>, "26 Oct 2026, 7:30 PM" and <span class="rr-ref">ORD-001257</span>. Use the formatter classes, never format inline.</li>
                <li>Say it in words: "Table 3 for 2 people", not "Table 3 · 2 people".</li>
                <li>Name things the way people know them: "My orders", "Order queue", not "Order entities".</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="buttons">
    <h2>Buttons</h2>
    <div class="sg-demo d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Book table</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Back to my reservations</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-danger">Cancel booking</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger">Cancel this booking</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Confirm</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm">Edit</button>
        <a href="#buttons">A plain link</a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3 mb-0">One <code>btn-primary</code> per view: the thing most people came to do. Everything else is <code>btn-outline-secondary</code>. Cancelling uses <code>btn-outline-danger</code>, and <code>btn-danger</code> only on the page that confirms it. Use <code>btn-sm</code> for actions on a row.</p>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="status">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">A status pill is <code>&lt;span class="rr-status rr-status--good"&gt;Confirmed&lt;/span&gt;</code>. The modifier is what the status means, so each module maps its own statuses onto the same six.</p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table align-middle mb-0">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Modifier</th><th>Means</th><th>Orders</th><th>Reservations</th><th>Payments (suggested)</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>--attention</code></td><td>Waiting for someone</td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Pending</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Pending</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Waiting at counter</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>--progress</code></td><td>Being worked on</td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--progress">Preparing</span></td><td></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--progress">Paying online</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>--good</code></td><td>Done well, ready</td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--good">Ready</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--good">Confirmed</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--good">Paid</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>--done</code></td><td>Finished</td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--done">Served</span> <span class="rr-status rr-status--done">Completed</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--done">Completed</span></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>--off</code></td><td>No longer happening</td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--off">Cancelled</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--off">Cancelled</span></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--off">Refunded</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>--bad</code></td><td>Went wrong</td><td></td><td></td><td><span class="rr-status rr-status--bad">Failed</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="forms">
    <h2>Forms</h2>
    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-lg-7">
            <div class="rr-panel">
                <div class="mb-4">
                    <label class="form-label" for="sg-date">Date</label>
                    <input class="form-control" id="sg-date" type="date" value="2026-10-26" style="max-width: 14rem" />
                </div>

                <fieldset class="mb-4">
                    <legend class="form-label fs-6">Seating</legend>
                    <div class="rr-tile-group">
                        <span class="rr-label mb-2">Lunch</span>
                        <div class="rr-tiles rr-tiles--wide">
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="sg-slot" id="sg-slot-1200" />
                            <label class="rr-tile" for="sg-slot-1200">12:00 PM</label>
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="sg-slot" id="sg-slot-1330" />
                            <label class="rr-tile" for="sg-slot-1330">1:30 PM</label>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rr-tile-group">
                        <span class="rr-label mb-2">Dinner</span>
                        <div class="rr-tiles rr-tiles--wide">
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="sg-slot" id="sg-slot-1800" />
                            <label class="rr-tile" for="sg-slot-1800">6:00 PM</label>
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="sg-slot" id="sg-slot-1930" checked />
                            <label class="rr-tile" for="sg-slot-1930">7:30 PM</label>
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="sg-slot" id="sg-slot-2100" />
                            <label class="rr-tile" for="sg-slot-2100">9:00 PM</label>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </fieldset>

                <fieldset class="mb-4">
                    <legend class="form-label fs-6">Table</legend>
                    <div class="rr-tiles">
                        @for (var table = 1; table <= 10; table++)
                        {
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="sg-table" id="sg-table-@table" checked="@(table == 3)" disabled="@(table == 5)" />
                            <label class="rr-tile" for="sg-table-@table">@table</label>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <div class="form-text">Table 5 shows the "taken" state.</div>
                </fieldset>

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <label class="form-label d-block" for="sg-party">Party size</label>
                    <div class="rr-stepper" data-stepper>
                        <button type="button" class="rr-stepper__button" data-step="-1" aria-label="One person fewer">&minus;</button>
                        <input class="rr-stepper__input" id="sg-party" type="number" value="2" min="1" max="20" />
                        <button type="button" class="rr-stepper__button" data-step="1" aria-label="One person more">+</button>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <label class="form-label" for="sg-request">Special request (optional)</label>
                    <textarea class="form-control is-invalid" id="sg-request" rows="2">A table by the window, a high chair, and a birthday cake at 8 pm with candles, please ...</textarea>
                    <div class="invalid-feedback">Keep the special request to 500 characters or fewer.</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-5">
            <ul class="sg-rules">
                <li><strong>Choice tiles</strong> (<code>rr-tiles</code> + <code>rr-tile</code>) replace dropdowns when there are a few options people compare: seatings, tables, payment methods. Each tile is a real radio button (<code>btn-check</code>), so the form sends it like any other field.</li>
                <li><strong>Steppers</strong> (<code>rr-stepper</code> with <code>data-stepper</code>) are for small counts: party size, quantities. The number stays a real input people can type into. Add <code>wwwroot/js/stepper.js</code> to the page's scripts.</li>
                <li>Every field has a visible label. Optional fields say "(optional)"; required ones say nothing.</li>
                <li>Validation messages sit under the field, in sambal, and say how to fix it. Fields that fail ASP.NET validation turn red by themselves (<code>input-validation-error</code>), tiles and steppers included.</li>
                <li>A form's buttons go in <code>rr-actionbar</code>, straight inside the form. On a phone it stays at the bottom of the screen.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="dockets">
    <h2>Dockets</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">The signature. A docket is <code>rr-docket</code>: a head (title, reference, status), lines (<code>rr-docket__line</code> with quantity, item, amount), a dashed tear line before the total, then the next step.</p>
    <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <span class="rr-label mb-3">In the kitchen</span>
            <article class="rr-docket">
                <div class="rr-docket__head">
                    <div>
                        <span class="rr-docket__title">Table 4</span>
                        <span class="rr-ref d-block">ORD-001256</span>
                        <span class="small text-muted">9:08 PM, 12 min ago</span>
                    </div>
                    <span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Pending</span>
                </div>
                <ol class="rr-docket__lines">
                    <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">2 ×</span> <span>Nasi Lemak</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount">RM 25.80</span></li>
                    <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">3 ×</span> <span>Teh Tarik</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount">RM 11.40</span></li>
                </ol>
                <div class="rr-docket__total"><span>Total</span><span class="rr-money">RM 37.20</span></div>
                <div class="rr-docket__meta"><span class="rr-status rr-status--off">Not paid</span></div>
                <div class="rr-docket__actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Start preparing</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-danger">Cancel</button>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
            <span class="rr-label mb-3">For the customer</span>
            <article class="rr-docket">
                <div class="rr-docket__head">
                    <div>
                        <span class="rr-docket__title">Table 6</span>
                        <span class="rr-ref d-block">ORD-001257</span>
                        <span class="small text-muted">Placed 25 Oct 2026, 9:08 PM</span>
                    </div>
                    <span class="rr-status rr-status--progress">Preparing</span>
                </div>
                <ol class="rr-steps mb-4" aria-label="Order progress">
                    <li class="is-done">Pending</li>
                    <li class="is-current" aria-current="step">Preparing</li>
                    <li>Ready</li>
                    <li>Served</li>
                </ol>
                <ol class="rr-docket__lines">
                    <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">1 ×</span> <span>Char Kway Teow</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount">RM 13.90</span></li>
                    <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">2 ×</span> <span>Cendol</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount">RM 13.00</span></li>
                </ol>
                <div class="rr-docket__total"><span>Total</span><span class="rr-money">RM 26.90</span></div>
                <div class="rr-docket__actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Go to payment</button>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-xl-4">
            <ul class="sg-rules">
                <li>Use a docket for a record a person hands over or receives: an order, a booking, a payment receipt.</li>
                <li>Not for navigation or settings. Those are plain cards (<code>rr-feature</code>, <code>rr-panel</code>).</li>
                <li>A docket on its own on a page gets <code>rr-docket--narrow</code>, so it keeps the width of a paper slip.</li>
                <li>A ticket left on the rail from an earlier day shows its date and time ("28 Oct, 9:33 PM"), not hours waiting.</li>
                <li>The steps line (<code>rr-steps</code>) shows where something is in a fixed journey. It doesn't update by itself.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="board">
    <h2>Order rail</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">For staff boards: <code>rr-board</code> holds columns (<code>rr-board__column</code>), each with a title and count, a steel rail, and dockets hanging from it. Four columns on a wide screen, two on a tablet, one on a phone.</p>
    <div class="rr-board">
        <section class="rr-board__column" aria-label="Pending">
            <h3 class="rr-board__title">Pending <span class="rr-count">1</span></h3>
            <div class="rr-board__rail"></div>
            <div class="rr-board__dockets">
                <article class="rr-docket">
                    <div class="rr-docket__head"><div><span class="rr-docket__title">Table 4</span><span class="rr-ref d-block">ORD-001256</span></div></div>
                    <ol class="rr-docket__lines">
                        <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">2 ×</span> <span>Nasi Lemak</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount"></span></li>
                        <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">3 ×</span> <span>Teh Tarik</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount"></span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <div class="rr-docket__actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Start preparing</button></div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="rr-board__column" aria-label="Preparing">
            <h3 class="rr-board__title">Preparing <span class="rr-count">1</span></h3>
            <div class="rr-board__rail"></div>
            <div class="rr-board__dockets">
                <article class="rr-docket">
                    <div class="rr-docket__head"><div><span class="rr-docket__title">Table 6</span><span class="rr-ref d-block">ORD-001257</span></div></div>
                    <ol class="rr-docket__lines">
                        <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">1 ×</span> <span>Char Kway Teow</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount"></span></li>
                        <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">2 ×</span> <span>Cendol</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount"></span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <div class="rr-docket__actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Mark ready</button></div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="rr-board__column" aria-label="Ready">
            <h3 class="rr-board__title">Ready <span class="rr-count">1</span></h3>
            <div class="rr-board__rail"></div>
            <div class="rr-board__dockets">
                <article class="rr-docket">
                    <div class="rr-docket__head"><div><span class="rr-docket__title">Table 2</span><span class="rr-ref d-block">ORD-001258</span></div></div>
                    <ol class="rr-docket__lines">
                        <li class="rr-docket__line"><span class="rr-docket__qty">3 ×</span> <span>Roti Canai (2 pieces)</span> <span class="rr-docket__amount"></span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <div class="rr-docket__actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Mark served</button></div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="rr-board__column" aria-label="Served">
            <h3 class="rr-board__title">Served <span class="rr-count">0</span></h3>
            <div class="rr-board__rail"></div>
            <p class="rr-board__empty">Nothing served yet.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="lists">
    <h2>Lists</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">A record in a customer's list is a slip (<code>rr-slip</code>): the details on the left, the status and actions on the right. A booking starts with a date block (<code>rr-dateblock</code>, a <code>&lt;time&gt;</code>), so people see the day before anything else, and <code>rr-slip__title--lead</code> sets the time (or an order's table) large. Buttons on a row carry the reference in a <code>visually-hidden</code> span, so a screen reader knows which one they're for.</p>
    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-xl-6">
            <ul class="list-unstyled d-grid gap-3 mb-0">
                <li class="rr-slip">
                    <time class="rr-dateblock" datetime="2026-10-26"><span class="rr-dateblock__day">Mon</span><span class="rr-dateblock__date">26</span><span class="rr-dateblock__month">Oct</span></time>
                    <div class="rr-slip__body">
                        <div>
                            <span class="rr-slip__title rr-slip__title--lead">7:30 PM</span>
                            <span class="d-block fw-semibold">Table 3 for 2 people</span>
                            <span class="rr-ref">RES-001840</span>
                            <p class="small text-muted mt-1 mb-0">Window seat please, it is our anniversary</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="rr-slip__side">
                            <span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Pending</span>
                            <div class="d-flex gap-2">
                                <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="#lists">Change<span class="visually-hidden"> RES-001840</span></a>
                                <a class="btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm" href="#lists">Cancel<span class="visually-hidden"> RES-001840</span></a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="rr-slip">
                    <div class="rr-slip__body">
                        <div>
                            <span class="rr-slip__title rr-slip__title--lead">Table 4</span>
                            <span class="d-block fw-semibold">5 items, <span class="rr-money">RM 37.20</span></span>
                            <div class="rr-row-meta"><span class="rr-ref">ORD-001256</span><span>25 Oct 2026, 9:08 PM</span></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="rr-slip__side">
                            <span class="rr-status rr-status--progress">Preparing</span>
                            <div class="d-flex gap-2">
                                <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="#lists">Payment<span class="visually-hidden"> for ORD-001256</span></a>
                                <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="#lists">View<span class="visually-hidden"> ORD-001256</span></a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-xl-6">
            <ul class="rr-dishes">
                <li class="rr-dish is-chosen">
                    <label for="sg-dish-1"><span class="rr-dish__name">Nasi Lemak</span><span class="rr-dish__price">RM 12.90</span></label>
                    <div class="rr-stepper" data-stepper>
                        <button type="button" class="rr-stepper__button" data-step="-1" aria-label="One less Nasi Lemak">&minus;</button>
                        <input class="rr-stepper__input" id="sg-dish-1" type="number" value="2" min="0" max="20" />
                        <button type="button" class="rr-stepper__button" data-step="1" aria-label="One more Nasi Lemak">+</button>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="rr-dish">
                    <label for="sg-dish-2"><span class="rr-dish__name">Teh Tarik</span><span class="rr-dish__price">RM 3.80</span></label>
                    <div class="rr-stepper" data-stepper>
                        <button type="button" class="rr-stepper__button" data-step="-1" aria-label="One less Teh Tarik">&minus;</button>
                        <input class="rr-stepper__input" id="sg-dish-2" type="number" value="0" min="0" max="20" />
                        <button type="button" class="rr-stepper__button" data-step="1" aria-label="One more Teh Tarik">+</button>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-muted mt-2 mb-0">Dish rows (<code>rr-dishes</code> + <code>rr-dish</code>) list what can be ordered. A chosen dish gets <code>is-chosen</code>, which the order page's script sets.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="dashboards">
    <h2>Dashboards</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">A dashboard leads with what the role needs now, made from real data: dockets for a customer's next table and order, a tally for staff, facts for an Admin. The shelf of everything else comes after.</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Tally</h3>
    <div class="rr-tally" role="group" aria-label="Kitchen">
        <a class="rr-tally__item is-attention" href="#dashboards"><span class="rr-tally__count">3</span><span class="rr-tally__label">new orders</span></a>
        <a class="rr-tally__item" href="#dashboards"><span class="rr-tally__count">1</span><span class="rr-tally__label">being prepared</span></a>
        <a class="rr-tally__item" href="#dashboards"><span class="rr-tally__count">1</span><span class="rr-tally__label">ready to serve</span></a>
        <a class="rr-tally__item" href="#dashboards"><span class="rr-tally__count">0</span><span class="rr-tally__label">served, not completed</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">Counts that need someone (<code>rr-tally</code>, <code>rr-tally__item</code>), each a link to the list behind it. A count waiting for someone gets <code>is-attention</code>, the kaya top edge. <code>rr-tally--one</code> holds a single count.</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Facts</h3>
    <div class="rr-panel">
        <dl class="rr-facts">
            <div class="rr-facts__item"><dt>Tables</dt><dd>10 tables in 1 dining area</dd><dd><a href="#dashboards">Tables</a></dd></div>
            <div class="rr-facts__item"><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Closed on Mondays</dd><dd><a href="#dashboards">Opening hours</a></dd></div>
            <div class="rr-facts__item is-attention"><dt>Menu</dt><dd>9 dishes, 0 available</dd><dd><a href="#dashboards">Menu items</a></dd></div>
            <div class="rr-facts__item"><dt>Online</dt><dd>Taking bookings, taking orders</dd><dd><a href="#dashboards">Restaurant details</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">How something is set up, as plain statements (<code>rr-facts</code>), each with the page that changes it. A fact that stops the restaurant working gets <code>is-attention</code>.</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Shelf</h3>
    <div class="rr-shelf">
        <div class="rr-shelf__sheet">
            <ul class="rr-shelf__list">
                <li class="rr-feature"><h4 class="rr-feature__title"><a href="#dashboards">Reservations</a></h4><p class="rr-feature__meta">Book, change or cancel a table.</p></li>
                <li class="rr-feature"><h4 class="rr-feature__title"><a href="#dashboards">Place orders</a></h4><p class="rr-feature__meta">Order food and drinks to your table.</p></li>
                <li class="rr-feature"><h4 class="rr-feature__title"><a href="#dashboards">Browse menu</a></h4><p class="rr-feature__meta">See what's on the menu.</p></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rr-shelf__soon">
            <button type="button" class="rr-feature rr-feature--soon"><span class="rr-feature__title">Feedback</span><span class="rr-soon">Coming soon</span></button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">A role's features (<code>rr-shelf</code>, built by <code>Pages/Dashboards/_Cards.cshtml</code>): one white sheet of <code>rr-feature</code> links, and the ones not built yet as quieter "Coming soon" buttons that do nothing. A plain <code>rr-feature</code> card outside a shelf still works for other pages.</p>
</section>

<section class="sg-section" id="pieces">
    <h2>Page pieces</h2>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Page header</h3>
    <div class="sg-demo">
        <div class="rr-page-header mb-0">
            <div>
                <div class="h1 mb-0">My reservations</div>
                <p class="rr-lede">Your upcoming bookings. Change or cancel them up to the seating.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rr-page-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Book a table</button></div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">Every page starts with <code>rr-page-header</code>: the title, one line of context if it helps, and the page's main action on the right.</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Filters</h3>
    <div class="sg-demo">
        <nav class="nav nav-pills" aria-label="Status">
            <a class="nav-link active" aria-current="page" href="#pieces">All</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="#pieces">Pending</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="#pieces">Confirmed</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="#pieces">Cancelled</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="#pieces">Completed</a>
        </nav>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">Filters are <code>nav-pills</code> links, so the choice is in the address and one tap applies it. No "Show" button.</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Messages</h3>
    <div class="d-grid gap-2">
        <div class="alert alert-success mb-0" role="status">Your reservation has been updated.</div>
        <div class="alert alert-warning mb-0" role="status">Your booking was confirmed, so the change needs confirming again.</div>
        <div class="alert alert-danger mb-0" role="alert">That table is already booked for this seating. Choose another time or table.</div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Empty state</h3>
    <div class="rr-empty">
        <p class="rr-empty__title">No upcoming reservations</p>
        <p class="mb-0">Book a table and it will show up here.</p>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Book a table</button>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">An empty list says what will appear and how to add the first one.</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Staff list</h3>
    <section aria-labelledby="sg-seating">
        <h4 class="rr-group-title" id="sg-seating">7:30 PM <span class="rr-count">2</span></h4>
        <ul class="rr-list">
            <li class="rr-list__item is-attention">
                <div class="rr-tableno"><span class="rr-label">Table</span> <span class="rr-tableno__number">3</span></div>
                <div class="rr-list__main">
                    <div class="fw-semibold">2 people</div>
                    <div class="rr-row-meta"><span>Customer #1</span><span class="rr-ref">RES-001840</span></div>
                    <p class="small text-muted mt-1 mb-0">Window seat please, it is our anniversary</p>
                </div>
                <span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Pending</span>
                <div class="rr-list__actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-success">Confirm</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger">Cancel</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">Edit</button>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="rr-list__item">
                <div class="rr-tableno"><span class="rr-label">Table</span> <span class="rr-tableno__number">7</span></div>
                <div class="rr-list__main">
                    <div class="fw-semibold">4 people</div>
                    <div class="rr-row-meta"><span>Customer #2</span><span class="rr-ref">RES-001843</span></div>
                </div>
                <span class="rr-status rr-status--good">Confirmed</span>
                <div class="rr-list__actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger">Cancel</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">Edit</button>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <p class="text-muted mt-2">For staff lists that people work through: <code>rr-list</code> rows, grouped under an <code>rr-group-title</code> with an <code>rr-count</code>. A row waiting for someone gets <code>is-attention</code> (the kaya edge).</p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Staff table</h3>
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table align-middle">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Time</th><th>Table</th><th>Party</th><th>Customer</th><th>Status</th><th><span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>6:00 PM<br /><span class="rr-ref">RES-001842</span></td><td>Table 2</td><td>6 people</td><td>Customer #9001</td>
                    <td><span class="rr-status rr-status--attention">Pending</span></td>
                    <td class="text-end text-nowrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Confirm</button> <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm">Cancel</button></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>7:30 PM<br /><span class="rr-ref">RES-001840</span></td><td>Table 3</td><td>2 people</td><td>Customer #1</td>
                    <td><span class="rr-status rr-status--good">Confirmed</span></td>
                    <td class="text-end text-nowrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm">Cancel</button></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/js/stepper.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
}
